---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="About" description="A bit about Thomas Haene — where he's lived, what he's studying, and what he cares about.">
  <div class="about-header">
    <img
      class="portrait"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}thomas-haene.jpg`}
      alt="Thomas Haene"
      width="150"
      height="150"
    />
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
      <h1>About Me</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="lead">
    I'm Thomas Haene — a student currently pursuing a Masters of Electrical Engineering at the University of Toronto.
  </p>

    <h2>My Story</h2>
  <p>
    I've lived in three countries: born in Cambridge, UK, then New Brunswick, Canada, for
    elementary and middle school, and then Abu Dhabi, UAE, for high school. In Abu Dhabi I
    attended the
    <a href="https://www.nordangliaeducation.com/bis-abu-dhabi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      British International School Abu Dhabi
    </a>, earning my IGCSE certificate and an IB Diploma with a score of 41/45 - placing me in
    the top 1% of international students that year. The school wrote a
    <a href="https://www.nordangliaeducation.com/bis-abu-dhabi/news/2021/08/05/meet-thomas-haene-class-of-2021-ib-diploma-graduate" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      profile piece
    </a> about me when I graduated.
  </p>
  <p>
    After high school I moved to Montreal to pursue a Bachelor's in Electrical Engineering at
    McGill University, ranked 30th globally by the QS World University Rankings 2027. I
    graduated in December 2025, and I'm now completing a Master's at the University of Toronto,
    finishing in December 2026.
  </p>

  
  <h2>Career Goals &amp; Aspirations</h2>
  <p>
    While the future may be uncertain, I know I want to build a career in wireless
    communications. The transmission of information over vast distances — often at frequencies
    far beyond human perception — feels almost magical to me, and my goal is to understand the
    underlying physics and engineering well enough to contribute something meaningful to the
    field.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm equally fascinated by space exploration and the work of the world's space agencies. The
    two interests are closer than they might seem: every image returned from a probe and every
    command sent to a rover depends on a radio link stretching across millions of kilometres.
    Combining those passions one day — working on the communication systems that make space
    missions possible — is exactly the kind of work I'd love to do.
  </p>

  <h2>My Hobbies &amp; Interests</h2>
  <p>
    Outside of the classroom, my main hobbies are basketball, weight-lifting, and drawing. I
    also write and make videos about things that fascinate me — you'll find the articles on the
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}blog/`}>blog</a> here, and the videos on my
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@TelecomTomTV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      YouTube channel
    </a>.
  </p>

</Layout>
